Ticket #4471 merged 412 reports of dates landing on the wrong day. The problem: the parser
reads dates as MM/DD (US format) when users in EU locales expect DD/MM.

We split #4471 into 31 issues, one per locale-tenant pair, so the desk can track fixes and
report coverage.

<Callout>
31 issues filed. Parser reads MM/DD when locale expects DD/MM.
</Callout>

## The problem

The date parser does not respect locale-specific formatting. When a user in an EU locale (en-GB,
pl-PL, it-IT, nl-NL, fr-FR, cs-CZ, da-DK, pt-PT, es-ES, de-DE, en-IE) enters a date as
DD/MM, the parser reads it as MM/DD. The month and day swap.

Example: user in nl-NL locale enters "12 May" (12/05), parser reads it as 5 December (05/12).

